§§ `The default: a fall is declined where the readings differ`

-- 2015: the amount denominated for 2015, whatever the reading.
#ASSERT (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2015)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2015)'s `under paragraph (2)(b)` EQUALS 188
#ASSERT (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2015)'s `under paragraph (2)(c)` EQUALS 140
-- 2016: the index fell. 150 left as it was is 150; lowered by 0.897% it is 148.65, rounded 149: they differ.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2016)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`
-- Every later year rests on 2016: declined, 2024 and 2026 included.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2018)'s `under paragraph (2)(b)`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2024)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2025)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2026)'s `under paragraph (2)(c)`

§§ `Outside the clause as encoded`

-- Before 2015 the amounts are not denominated; after 2026 the November 2026 index is not in the CBS file.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2014)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` 2027)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`

§§ `One update, directly`

-- A rise: 169 x 1.02361 = 172.99 -> 173; the 1 January 2026 readings, any reading of a fall.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` `the readings this row takes` `:` 169 `updated on 1 January of` 2026 EQUALS 173
-- A fall (1 January 2021, 100.2/100.8): 152 stays 152 on the first reading, becomes 151 on the second (152 x 0.99405
-- = 151.10), and is declined by default.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` `read as` `a fall in the index leaves the basic amount unchanged`) `:` 152 `updated on 1 January of` 2021 EQUALS 152
#ASSERT `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` `read as` `a fall in the index lowers the basic amount by the fall`) `:` 152 `updated on 1 January of` 2021 EQUALS 151
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` `the readings this row takes` `:` 152 `updated on 1 January of` 2021
-- A fall too small to change the rounded amount: 1 January 2017 (98.9/99.2 = 0.99698): 100 x 0.99698 = 99.70 -> 100,
-- the same as 100 left: the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` `the readings this row takes` `:` 100 `updated on 1 January of` 2017 EQUALS 100

§§ `The CBS twelve-month change gives the same amounts as the index ratio (fork U2)`

-- The third number of each year's readings is the CBS's own twelve-month change in percent. Used instead of the
-- ratio, with the same rounding, it gives the same amount in every year 2015 to 2026 (checked below by an
-- independent recursion, on the reading that a fall leaves the amount as it was).
GIVEN nominal IS A NUMBER
      year    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount by the CBS percentage, denominated as` nominal `, on 1 January of` year MEANS
    IF   year EQUALS 2015
    THEN nominal
    ELSE IF   year EQUALS 2025
         THEN `the amount by the CBS percentage, denominated as` nominal `, on 1 January of` 2024
         ELSE IF   change LESS THAN 0
              THEN `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` previous
              ELSE `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (previous TIMES (1 PLUS (change DIVIDED BY 100)))
    WHERE
        previous MEANS `the amount by the CBS percentage, denominated as` nominal `, on 1 January of` (year MINUS 1)
        change   MEANS (`the CBS index readings for the update of 1 January of` year)'s `the twelve-month change the CBS published with the later reading, in percent`
